{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "Scope: The contract specifies the population as all patients after deduplication, but the analyst further excluded rows with biomarker_baseline == -999, reducing the sample to 712 patients. This deviates from the defined estimand population.",
    "Overreach: The answer presents the result as a \"treatment effect\" implying causality, yet only severity was adjusted for. Other potential confounders (age, sex, site, assay_batch) remain unaddressed, so a causal interpretation is unwarranted.",
    "Unacknowledged data problems: The exclusion of -999 sentinel values is not justified or discussed; if missingness is informative, the standardised estimate may be biased. The severity distribution used for standardisation is based on the filtered dataset, not the full deduplicated cohort."
  ]
}
